  people hostage is very different because  this is a wakandan ship we see the  wakandan markings and Technology on the  walls and these soldiers that we see  here are most likely mercenaries guns  for hire most likely hired by somebody  who is searching for vibranium could be  another government it could be somebody  like Dr Doom either way whoever's behind  this wants vibranium but little did they  know that the Dora milaje were actually  Undercover on this ship now this is  where the war kind of begins or at least  picks up because we might be safe to  assume that wakanda and telecom have had  their beef with each other for some time  now just like in the car Comics but  these people searching for vibranium in  his oceans is kind of where it picks up  again this is where the tension really  starts to rise and this is where we see  queen raimonda and the door milage  actually visit imbaku where we hear  imbaku telling them his people do not  call him general or King they call him  kukul Khan the feather serpent God now  as he says this we actually see a shot  of Namor being born in the water we can  see the feathers on his feet and then  they show a shot of him grown up  feathers on his feet flying in the air  with wakanda in the background then we  hear umbaku say killing him will risk  Eternal War so this tells us that not  only is Namor the king of Atlantis slash  Telecom but he is worshiped as their God  not just their King but their God now  cool cool Khan is actually an ancient  Mexican Pantheon a deity one of the  major deities so this is coming straight  from ancient Mexican history here which  I love now umbaku says killing him will  risk Eternal War because if they kill  the the god of telecon of course taliken  will forever try to kill everybody in  wakanda to seek revenge on them for  killing their God which puts them in  quite the Dilemma because clearly Namor  is attacking wakanda we hear shuri say  he's coming for the surface world and in  this scene we see Queen raimonda and we  actually see Riri Williams in the  background in the throne room they are  looking out the window and if you notice  in the reflection of the window is name  or flying right in front of it and it  looks like he's about to take a spear  and shove it right through the window  breaking the glass breaking into the  throne room maybe even attacking Queen  raimonda now from here in the trailer we  actually see Namor on land talking to  Queen raimonda and I'm assuming that  this is one of two things happening one  it's Namor coming to the surface to kind  of say sorry to Quinn ramunda for the  death of t'challa their King and her son  or two he is coming on Surface to warn  her and express that he is extremely  upset that wakanda has let the world  know about vibranium and now people are  invading his seas and most likely  telling her that he won wants her to  shut off wakanda and vibranium to the  world to where nobody can even get close  which obviously I don't think she was  going to do this was the wish of her son  and the former king of wakanda t'challa  so I don't think she's going to go back  on what he did when he was alive and  that is also where the conflict is going  to escalate as well Namor issues of  warning but Rwanda says no now from here  we get a bunch of shots of what is going  to be the war between telekin and  wakanda and from here we get some really  cool scenes one we get our first look at  Riri Williams's Iron Heart In Action we  see her very first Iron Heart suit in a  couple of scenes we see her flying over  a car and a motorcycle we see her  tinkering with some gear to make her  suit and then we see her suit launch  into the sky and we even get a hood view  of her saying let's go and this is very  similar to the Views that we saw of Iron  Man when he would be in the suit now we  see wakanda being flooded of course this  is the doing of Namor he is attacked  wakanda the war has begun and in the  background you may n